========================== Q24 ==============================

Will this compile?

interface A {
    void show(int x);
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A a = x -> {
            int x = 20;
            System.out.println(x);
        };
    }
}

ANSWER:
NO — Compile-time error.

Reason:
x is already the lambda parameter.

You cannot declare another local variable
with the same name x inside the lambda body.
